{"name":"Starglider","hex":"#faeede","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Starglider","blocks":[{"text":"Starglider is a 3D video game published in 1986 by Rainbird. It was developed by Jez San under his company name Argonaut Software. The game is a fast-moving, first-person combat flight simulator, rendered with colourful wireframe vector graphics inspired by San's love of the 1983 Atari coin-op Star Wars."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/52/Starglider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starglider","wikidata":"Q3195863"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/Starglider_screenshot.png/250px-Starglider_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b6/Starglider_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/b6/Starglider_screenshot.png/250px-Starglider_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cockpit view. A walker robot is on-screen. Amiga version.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarglider_screenshot.png"}],"sounds":{}}}